{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>ואספו אספה [אסיר]</b> (And they will be gathered, a gathering [of prisoners]). Like prisoners: as when a multitude of prisoners is brought into a pit to be locked up, and they leave them there many days. And likewise 'they will be visited' — to give them sustenance. The meaning is that this evil will persist. It is also possible that it is like ומימים רבים תפקד (Ezekiel 38:8), and this visitation is for evil."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:01.741378066Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}